  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Arab Fund for Arts and Culture, AFAC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Arab Documentary Photography Program, ADPP, and The AFAC Documetary Program, ADP, to independent artists and cultural institutions in the Arab region in support of creative expression, freedom of expression, mobility and exchange. The project has a clear focus on measures to counteract rising conservatism and a backlash against cultural activists, including those highlighting women&#x2019;s rights and gender equality.

The AFAC Documetary Program, ADP, offers support to creative documentaries. AFAC welcomes, on an annual basis, submissions of feature-length, medium length and short documentaries in the development, production and post- production phases. It aims to build on AFAC&#x2019;s dedication to documentary film by supporting established and emerging Arab documentary filmmakers that are addressing the social realities of a changing Arab world in creative and compelling ways. 

Arab Documentary Photography Program, ADPP, was launched in 2014. Its objectives are to raise the level of creative documentary photography in the Arab region; to train photographers and expand their approaches to visual storytelling; to share strong visual narratives from the Arab region regionally and internationally; and to explore wider access to documentary photography and a more active engagement with its audiences. ADPP encompasses not only a grant but also training and one-on-one mentorship to accompany the photographers in articulating their photo stories. .</narrative>
  </description>
